==============================================================================================================================
0.  RUN g06 ITSELF AND WORK ON ITS OWN OBJECTS (no re-implementation, so no transcription error)
==============================================================================================================================
  g06 executed in-process, exit code 1 (5 of its own checks FAIL)
  g06's primary median boost, recomputed here: canonical 0.817, alt 0.746

==============================================================================================================================
1.  THE ARITHMETIC.  Re-derive every number in the claim from scratch and demand it match
==============================================================================================================================
      direct baryonic sum          g_N = 6.0245e-15 m/s^2 = 0.000064 a_0   (claim 6.02e-15)
      2M++ reconstruction          g   = 1.1608e-12 m/s^2 = 0.012401 a_0   (claim 1.161e-12)
      bisection inversion          g_N = 1.4219e-14;  independent deep-limit g^2/a_0 = 1.4395e-14 (differ by 1.2%, the exact-vs-deep kernel correction)
      ratio g_B/g_N,inv = 0.4237   (claim 0.42);   raw factor g_L/g_B = 192.7 (claim 193)
  [PASS] A1 the arithmetic of the claim is CORRECT.  The bisection inverts the kernel properly, the linear-theory reduction v = 2 f g/(3 H_0 Omega_m) is applied consistently (the growth rate cancels between the velocity prediction and the conversion back to g), and every quoted number reproduces.  If this failed the claim would die here on arithmetic; it does not, so the attack has to be on the ESTIMATOR and the PREMISE   (g_B 6.0245e-15, g_L 1.1608e-12, ratio 0.4237, deep-limit inversion agrees to 1.2%)

==============================================================================================================================
2.  THE 'SUPPORTING CROSS-CHECK' IS THE SAME NUMBER.  620 km/s adds nothing that E1 did not already say
==============================================================================================================================
      baryons through nu, v ~ g t_0 : 328 km/s        (g06 prints 328)
      2M++ field, v ~ g t_0         : 505 km/s        (g06 prints 505)
      CMB dipole (Local Group)      : 620 km/s   (Planck 2018 VI / Kogut+1993)
      but in the deep limit g_N = g_MOND^2/a_0 EXACTLY, so   (nu(g_B) g_B / g_L)^2 = 0.4219
      and E1's ratio                                          g_B / g_N,inv       = 0.4237
  [FAIL] A2 the velocity cross-check offered in support of E1 is NOT independent of E1.  Because the kernel is deep at these accelerations, g_N = g_MOND^2/a_0 exactly, so the ratio of the two ROUTES' Newtonian fields is the SQUARE of the ratio of their predicted velocities.  Quoting 328 vs 505 km/s beside a ratio of 0.42 is quoting one number twice.  This check asserts the two are independent (differ by more than 5%), and it fails.  What the velocities DO add is a comparison against 620 km/s -- and there the baryonic route is 1.9x short while the reconstruction is 1.2x short, so that comparison mildly favours the reconstruction's normalisation, not the baryonic sum's   ((nu(g_B)g_B/g_L)^2 = 0.4219 against E1's g_B/g_N,inv = 0.4237 -- the same quantity to 0.4%.  Against the 620 km/s dipole: baryons 1.89x short, reconstruction 1.23x short)

==============================================================================================================================
3.  E1 IS KNIFE-EDGE, AND IT FAILS INSIDE g06'S OWN STELLAR M/L BRACKET
==============================================================================================================================
     Upsilon_K   g_B (m/s^2)   g_B/g_N,inv   E1 (0.4 - 2.5)
           0.4     4.016e-15        0.2825             FAIL
           0.5     5.020e-15        0.3531             FAIL
           0.6     6.024e-15        0.4237             PASS
           0.8     8.033e-15        0.5649             PASS
           1.0     1.004e-14        0.7062             PASS
  (Upsilon_K scales the stellar mass in BOTH the 2MRS far term and the UNGC near term, so this is the
   honest one-parameter sensitivity of E1 to the single largest systematic g06 itself carries.)
  [FAIL] A3 E1 -- the check the whole rung is declared to rest on -- passes by 6% of its own threshold and FAILS at Upsilon_K = 0.4, which is not an invented value but the LOW END OF THE BRACKET g06 CARRIES IN ITS OWN SYSTEMATICS TABLE (where it is shown to move the median boost to 1.011).  A load-bearing check must survive the file's own declared systematics.  This asserts that; it fails   (Upsilon_K = 0.4 gives ratio 0.282 (E1 FAILS), 0.6 gives 0.424 (PASS, by 6% of the threshold), 1.0 gives 0.706 (PASS))

==============================================================================================================================
4.  THE ESTIMATOR: the Local Group number is a near-cancellation, and the two sides of E1 are not the
    same volume
==============================================================================================================================
      far term  (2MRS, r > 3 Mpc)  |g| = 1.0157e-14 toward (l, b) = (261, +45)
      near term (UNGC, r < 3 Mpc)  |g| = 1.0143e-14 toward (l, b) = (123, -33)
      the two are 145 degrees apart and nearly equal in size, so the quoted sum 6.024e-15 is 1.69x SMALLER than either term
      the near term's largest contributors, by g = G M / r^2:
          MESSIER031     M_b = 3.94e+10 Msun at 0.77 Mpc  ->  g = 9.256e-15 m/s^2
          SMC            M_b = 1.02e+09 Msun at 0.06 Mpc  ->  g = 6.313e-15 m/s^2
          MESSIER033     M_b = 4.86e+09 Msun at 0.85 Mpc  ->  g = 9.376e-16 m/s^2
          MAFFEI2        M_b = 2.89e+10 Msun at 2.80 Mpc  ->  g = 5.133e-16 m/s^2
      M31 is INSIDE the Local Group.  It does not source the Local Group barycentre's motion, and the
      2M++ side of the comparison excludes everything within 3 Mpc/h = 4.45 Mpc.  So E1 compares a sum
      that includes Local Group members against a reconstruction that excludes them.
      dropping the near term (the volume-matched comparison): ratio = 0.714 instead of 0.424, and the predicted Local Group velocity rises to 426 km/s
  [FAIL] A4 the two sides of E1 are volume-matched.  They are not: the baryonic sum runs from 0 Mpc outward and is half-cancelled by an M31-dominated near term that lies INSIDE the Local Group, while the 2M++ side is cut at 3 Mpc/h.  This check asserts the quoted sum is not dominated by that cancellation -- that dropping the unmatched near term moves the ratio by less than 20%.  It fails.  NOTE THE DIRECTION: the volume-matched number is BETTER for the claim, so this is an error in g06's own disfavour   (as quoted 0.424; volume-matched (far term only) 0.714, a factor 1.69; the two terms cancel at 145 degrees)
  
      2MRS is cut at cz > 350 km/s, i.e. d > 5.36 Mpc; the UNGC is used only inside R_SEAM = 3.0 Mpc.
      So the shell 3.0 - 5.36 Mpc contributes NOTHING to the baryonic external field, and it holds 207 UNGC galaxies
      (M81 3.63, NGC 5128 3.75, NGC 4945 3.80, NGC 253 3.94, NGC 4736 4.66, NGC 5236 4.92 Mpc all sit in the hole).
      Their summed vector field at the Local Group is 9.933e-16 m/s^2, i.e. 0.16x the quoted total.
  [PASS] A5 (ATTACK ATTEMPTED, ATTACK FAILED -- reported anyway) the baryonic external field has a real gap in its radial coverage: a 3.00 - 5.36 Mpc shell is sampled by neither catalogue, and it contains M81, Cen A, NGC 253, NGC 4945, NGC 4736 and NGC 5236.  This check asserts the gap is worth less than 30% of the quoted total, i.e. that it does not matter.  It PASSES: 207 galaxies spread over the sky largely cancel, and the residual is 16%.  So the gap is a defect in the estimator but not a lever on the answer, and filling it would in any case RAISE the baryonic field and move E1 toward agreement   (207 UNGC galaxies in the unsampled 3.00 - 5.36 Mpc shell contribute 9.933e-16 m/s^2 = 0.16x the quoted 6.024e-15)

==============================================================================================================================
5.  AN INDEPENDENT NORMALISATION OF THE FAR TERM -- and it is FOR the claim, not against it
==============================================================================================================================
  If light traced mass, the Newtonian field of stars-plus-cold-gas would be Omega_(*+cold)/Omega_m times
  the total-matter field the 2M++ reconstruction returns.  Fukugita & Peebles 2004 give Omega_(*+cold) = 0.0034;
  Omega_m = 0.313 here, so that is 0.0108 x 1.161e-12 = 1.259e-14 m/s^2, against the 2MRS sum's 1.016e-14.
  [PASS] A6 (THIS ONE SUPPORTS THE CLAIM, and is checked as hard as the ones that do not) the 2MRS far-field sum is independently normalised.  Its magnitude is predicted to 20% by the cosmic stellar-plus-cold-gas density fraction times the 2M++ total-matter field.  So the magnitude-limited 2MRS sum is NOT badly incomplete for this purpose, and g06's 'lower bound, a threefold error is possible' caveat is if anything too generous to its critics.  The disagreement between the two routes is therefore NOT a data-quality problem; it is exactly the Omega_(*+cold)/Omega_m ratio, which is the real question   (2MRS sum 1.016e-14 vs Omega_(*+cold)/Omega_m x 2M++ = 1.259e-14, ratio 0.81)

==============================================================================================================================
6.  HOW BIG MUST THE EXTERNAL FIELD BE BEFORE THE RUNG'S ANSWER ACTUALLY REVERSES?
==============================================================================================================================
  g06 shows two points -- x1 (boost 0.817) and x3 (0.909) -- and the raw reconstruction (2.215).  The
  interesting question is the curve between them, because the candidate corrections are not factors of 3.
     g_ext multiplier  median e_N/a_0  boost canonical   boost alt  in cluster band?
                  1.0         0.00015            0.817       0.746                no
                  3.0         0.00045            0.909       0.831                no
                  6.4         0.00097            0.962       0.880                no
                 10.0         0.00152            1.085       0.990                no
                 14.5         0.00220            1.237       1.130                no
                 30.0         0.00455            1.531       1.401               YES
                 60.0         0.00909            1.890       1.731               YES
                100.0         0.01515            2.247       2.062               YES
                193.0         0.02924            2.855       2.626               YES
  the median boost first enters the liability table's cluster/group band (>= 1.45) at a multiplier of about 30 on the baryonic external field
  and reaches g06's own R1 threshold of 1.8 between 30x and 60x
  
  PURE-BARYON CEILING.  If ALL baryons (not just stars and cold gas) source the field, how large can the
  baryonic g_N be before the framework over-predicts the Local Group's own 620 km/s?  Solving
  nu(g_N/a_0) g_N t_0 = 620 km/s gives g_N = 2.138e-14 = 0.00023 a_0, i.e. 3.5x the direct sum,
  which is a median boost of 0.919 canonical / 0.840 alt.
  (For contrast: if all baryons traced the 2M++ structure, Omega_b/Omega_m = 0.157 x 1.161e-12 = 1.824e-13 = 30x the direct sum, which the 620 km/s
   dipole EXCLUDES -- it would predict 1837 km/s.  That over-prediction of bulk flows by
   MOND is a known separate liability and is not this rung's problem.)
  [PASS] A7 (ALSO FOR THE CLAIM) inside a strictly baryons-only reading the conclusion is ROBUST.  The Local Group's own measured 620 km/s caps the baryonic Newtonian field at a few times the direct sum, and at that cap the median boost is still far under the cluster band.  So no plausible error in COUNTING BARYONS reverses this rung.  This is the strongest thing that can be said for the claim and it is said here   (at the dipole cap (3.5x the direct sum) the median boost is 0.919 canonical / 0.840 alt, against the cluster band's 1.45)

==============================================================================================================================
7.  THE REFUTATION: the premise 'in this framework the actual matter is BARYONS' is not this repository's
    own standing
==============================================================================================================================
  g06 section 4, verbatim: 'In QUMOND the external-field parameter is e_N = |g_N,ext|/a_0 where g_N,ext is
  the NEWTONIAN field sourced by the actual matter.  In this framework the actual matter is BARYONS.'
  
  STANDING.md, section 5 item 5, verbatim: "'No dark matter' is forfeited.  The framework *has* a dark
  sector -- the AeST/ghost-condensate Q-mode, a gravity mode rather than a particle.  Honest framing:
  MOND galaxies **plus** a no-particle CDM-like sector."
  STANDING.md line 423: 'I_0 ~ Omega_dm is recorded as robustly free'.
  STANDING.md item 3 (the 09-02 mu-pincer): 'pressure cannot keep Omega_dm out of galaxies.'
  
  A CDM-like sector that clusters is a NEWTONIAN SOURCE.  If the framework's relativistic completion
  carries it -- and the repository's own standing says it does, at ~Omega_dm -- then the Newtonian field
  external to a Local Volume group is sourced by baryons PLUS that sector, which is what a LambdaCDM
  velocity-field reconstruction returns.  On that reading g06's 'wrong, shown' branch is the right one.
  
      external field = baryons only (g06 primary) ................ boost 0.817 / 0.746
      external field = total matter (2M++ raw, the dark-sector
        reading, which is g06's own R4b branch) .................. boost 2.215 / 2.030
      external field = 2M++ scaled by Omega_b/Omega_m (a sanity
        intermediate, no dark sector but all baryons) ............ boost 1.210
  [FAIL] A8 THE LOAD-BEARING PREMISE HOLDS.  It does not.  The claim's first half -- that nu's argument takes the Newtonian field of the actual matter -- is correct QUMOND and is not in dispute.  Its second half -- that the actual matter is BARYONS -- is contradicted by this repository's own STANDING.md, which forfeits 'no dark matter' and records a CDM-like ghost-condensate Q-mode at ~Omega_dm that the mu-pincer says cannot be kept out of galaxies.  With that sector sourcing the external field the rung lands at a median boost of 2.22, inside the cluster band -- which is g06's own R4b, the check it already fails on purpose.  So the rung's answer is CONDITIONAL on a premise the repository has already retracted, and 'the answer reverses if that is wrong' is not a hypothetical here   (STANDING.md item 5 forfeits 'no dark matter' and names the AeST/ghost-condensate Q-mode: found in STANDING.md = True.  Baryons-only boost 0.817; total-matter external field 2.215 canonical / 2.030 alt, i.e. +0.433 dex and inside the 1.45-3.45 cluster band)
  [FAIL] A9 the repository is self-consistent about which quantity the 2M++ reduction returns.  It is not: the committed h81_h82_mw_external_fields.py computes the IDENTICAL expression and calls it 'the NEWTONIAN large-scale field at the Local Group', and its check 81a is built on that reading ('in the Newtonian units the EFE actually uses, large-scale structure beats the LMC by about an order of magnitude').  g06 calls the same expression a MOND field.  Both are committed; they cannot both stand   (h81_h82 uses the same reduction and labels it Newtonian: True.  Under h81's reading e_N at the Local Group is 0.0124 a_0; under g06's it is 0.00006 a_0, a factor 193)

