8.  MUTATION CONTROLS ON THIS AUDIT
==============================================================================================================================
  [PASS] V-M1 mutation -- set the external field to exactly zero.  If the external field were doing the work attributed to it, this must move the answer; if the sensitivity curve of section 6 were an artefact of the gext_mult plumbing, zero would not sit at the isolated-branch value g06 already prints (0.706)   (gext_mult = 0 gives 0.706, against g06's independently computed isolated branch 0.706)
  [PASS] V-M2 the boost must rise monotonically with the external field, because a larger e_N pushes nu toward 1 and shrinks the predicted dispersion.  A non-monotone curve would mean the gext plumbing or the EFE branch is doing something other than advertised   (boosts across multipliers 1 -> 193: 0.82, 0.91, 0.96, 1.08, 1.24, 1.53, 1.89, 2.25, 2.86)
  [PASS] V-M3 mutation -- evaluate the 2M++ field somewhere other than the origin.  If g_lss_lcdm returned a position-independent constant (a plumbing bug), the whole R4b branch would be meaningless   (|g| at the origin 1.161e-12, at (3, 4, 5) Mpc 1.480e-12, ratio 1.275)
  [PASS] V-M4 both footings throughout: every boost in section 6 was computed on both a_0 and the verdict does not turn on the choice   (total-matter external field gives 2.215 canonical / 2.030 alt, +0.038 dex apart)

==============================================================================================================================
9.  VERDICT
==============================================================================================================================
  WHAT SURVIVES THE ATTACK
    * The arithmetic.  Every number in the claim reproduces (A1), the kernel inversion is right, and the
      linear-theory reduction is applied consistently.  No bug was found in the computation.
    * The 2MRS baryon sum's normalisation, independently confirmed to 20% (A6).
    * The claim's structural half: QUMOND's nu takes the Newtonian field of the actual matter.  True.
    * The robustness of the rung to any error in COUNTING BARYONS: the Local Group's own 620 km/s caps
      that at 3.5x and the boost only reaches 0.92 (A7).
  
  WHAT DOES NOT
    * The premise that the framework's matter is baryons (A8).  STANDING.md forfeits 'no dark matter' and
      carries a CDM-like Q-mode at ~Omega_dm.  With it, the external field IS the total-matter field, the
      rung reads 2.22, and the claim's own escape clause -- 'this rung's answer reverses if that is
      wrong' -- is triggered by the repository's own standing rather than by a hypothetical.
    * The evidence offered for the premise.  E1 fails inside g06's own Upsilon_K bracket (A3); its
      supporting velocity cross-check is E1 restated (A2); and the compared volumes do not match (A4, A5).
    * Repository self-consistency: h81_h82 reads the same number the opposite way (A9).
  
  WHAT THIS DOES NOT SHOW.  It does not show the baryonic reading is WRONG -- if the Q-mode is smooth on
  4-200 Mpc scales, or if I_0 is small, the baryonic reading is right and the rung stands at 0.82.  It
  shows the rung is CONDITIONAL on an unsettled premise that the repository has already retracted in the
  other direction, and that the conditionality is a factor 2.7 in the answer -- the difference between
  'groups do not look like clusters' and 'groups look exactly like clusters'.

